1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:07,880
Listen.

2
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,020
Practice.

3
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:09,900
Speak.

4
00:00:10,610 --> 00:00:12,250
Practice makes you perfect.

5
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:14,770
Hello, everyone.

6
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:18,030
Welcome to our Business English practice session.

7
00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:24,620
Today, we will learn how to introduce yourself in simple, clear English.

8
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:26,160
Explanation.

9
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:31,520
An introduction means telling people basic information about you.

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,600
Are you ready to practice?

11
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:35,300
Hi, everyone.

12
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:36,910
I'm excited you're here.

13
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:41,470
In business and daily life, you often need to talk about yourself.

14
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:42,930
Explanation.

15
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:47,740
You introduce yourself in interviews, meetings, and new workplaces.

16
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:53,880
We will talk slowly, explain everything, and help you repeat.

17
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:54,730
Great.

18
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:57,110
Let's begin with greetings.

19
00:00:58,070 --> 00:01:01,240
When you meet someone, you can say, Hello.

20
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:02,600
Nice to meet you.

21
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:04,360
Explanation.

22
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:06,920
This is polite and friendly.

23
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:08,560
Let's practice.

24
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:09,810
Hello.

25
00:01:10,590 --> 00:01:11,410
Nice to meet you.

26
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:13,290
Nice to meet you, too.

27
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:14,930
Explanation.

28
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:17,880
To means the same back to you.

29
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:19,940
Now you try at home.

30
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:22,120
So, first question.

31
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:24,000
What is your name?

32
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:25,210
Explanation.

33
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:27,640
Always start with your name.

34
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:30,100
My name is Daniel.

35
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:31,360
And you?

36
00:01:32,020 --> 00:01:32,700
What is your name?

37
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:34,480
My name is Sarah.

38
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,990
Explanation.

39
00:01:36,050 --> 00:01:40,110
Say, my name is not only Sarah.

40
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:41,910
It sounds more polite.

41
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:43,800
Let's repeat together.

42
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:46,820
My name is Sarah.

43
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,220
Wonderful.

44
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:54,010
When you introduce yourself, you can also say, I am Daniel.

45
00:01:54,430 --> 00:01:55,210
Explanation.

46
00:01:56,090 --> 00:02:00,930
I am is shorter and more casual, but both are correct.

47
00:02:01,570 --> 00:02:01,930
Yes.

48
00:02:02,610 --> 00:02:04,880
Some people say, I'm Sarah.

49
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:06,360
Explanation.

50
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,840
I'm is a contraction.

51
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:10,860
It is fast speech.

52
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:12,220
Repeat.

53
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:13,820
I'm Sarah.

54
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:16,490
Next, where are you from?

55
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:18,490
I'm from Canada.

56
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:20,010
Explanation.

57
00:02:20,730 --> 00:02:23,250
I'm from country, city.

58
00:02:24,130 --> 00:02:25,290
Where are you from?

59
00:02:25,310 --> 00:02:27,390
I'm from Australia.

60
00:02:27,410 --> 00:02:28,910
Explanation.

61
00:02:28,970 --> 00:02:32,200
Not I from Australia.

62
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,840
Remember the verb am.

63
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:35,940
Repeat.

64
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:38,070
I'm from Australia.

65
00:02:38,110 --> 00:02:40,990
Some people like to add a city.

66
00:02:41,730 --> 00:02:45,580
For example, I'm from Toronto, Canada.

67
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:48,420
Or, I'm from Sydney, Australia.

68
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:49,840
Very good.

69
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:51,950
Now, age.

70
00:02:52,950 --> 00:02:56,750
In business, you don't need to say your exact age.

71
00:02:57,670 --> 00:03:00,120
You can say, I'm in my 30s.

72
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,020
Or, I'm in my 20s.

73
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:04,380
Explanation.

74
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:08,880
This means an age range, more professional and private.

75
00:03:09,550 --> 00:03:09,790
Yes.

76
00:03:10,550 --> 00:03:10,770
Good.

77
00:03:11,590 --> 00:03:13,910
Next, what do you do?

78
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,780
This means your job or study.

79
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,520
I am a project manager.

80
00:03:20,410 --> 00:03:22,970
I manage teams and business tasks.

81
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:25,770
I am a marketing specialist.

82
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:28,960
I help promote products and services.

83
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:30,400
Explanation.

84
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:34,550
Use I am a before your job title.

85
00:03:35,270 --> 00:03:38,950
If you are a student, say I am a student.

86
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,640
I study business.

87
00:03:42,210 --> 00:03:44,290
or I study English.

88
00:03:44,890 --> 00:03:48,960
I study plus subject.

89
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,320
Let's ask about family.

90
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:54,860
Do you live alone or with family?

91
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:58,070
I live with my wife and our son.

92
00:03:58,130 --> 00:04:01,250
I live with my parents and my sister.

93
00:04:01,270 --> 00:04:06,600
I live with to describe people in your home.

94
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:10,750
Or you can say, I live by myself.

95
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,080
This means you live alone.

96
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:15,180
Now, hobbies.

97
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,800
What do you like to do in your free time?

98
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:20,150
I like cooking and reading.

99
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:24,270
I enjoy hiking and listening to music.

100
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:26,070
Explanation.

101
00:04:26,090 --> 00:04:31,020
I like and I enjoy both show hobbies.

102
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:32,760
Let's practice.

103
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:36,200
Say your hobbies now at home.

104
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:37,940
Very good.

105
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,770
Next, favorites.

106
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,160
What is your favorite food?

107
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:44,880
My favorite food is sushi.

108
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:48,070
My favorite food is pizza.

109
00:04:49,050 --> 00:04:49,730
Explanation.

110
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:53,270
Favorite means the one you like the best.

111
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:55,680
What is your favorite color?

112
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:58,560
My favorite color is blue.

113
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,350
My favorite color is green.

114
00:05:02,090 --> 00:05:03,610
What is your favorite animal?

115
00:05:04,730 --> 00:05:05,910
I like dogs.

116
00:05:06,850 --> 00:05:07,940
I like cats.

117
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,070
Also, talk about dislikes.

118
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:14,010
I don't like being late.

119
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:16,560
I dislike rude people.

120
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,080
Explanation.

121
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:24,170
I don't like and I dislike show negative preferences.

122
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:29,580
Now, let's combine everything into a natural introduction.

123
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:31,140
Listen first.

124
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,840
Hello, my name is Daniel.

125
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:36,930
I'm from Canada.

126
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,060
I'm in my 30s.

127
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,560
I am a project manager.

128
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:43,650
I live with my family.

129
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:46,610
Hello, everyone.

130
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:49,900
Welcome back to our Business English podcast.

131
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:56,230
Today, we are going to practice one very important question.

132
00:05:57,050 --> 00:05:58,390
Tell me about yourself.

133
00:06:00,410 --> 00:06:06,120
This question comes up in interviews, meetings, and even casual conversations.

134
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:12,130
Many people think it's easy, but it can be tricky if you don't prepare.

135
00:06:13,590 --> 00:06:14,250
Yes, David.

136
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:15,330
It's true.

137
00:06:16,130 --> 00:06:19,340
If you answer too short, people don't know much about you.

138
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,780
If you answer too long, it can be confusing.

139
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:28,170
So today, we'll show you a clear, simple, and friendly way to answer.

140
00:06:28,230 --> 00:06:30,330
Exactly.

141
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:32,940
Let's start at the very beginning.

142
00:06:35,010 --> 00:06:40,350
When someone asks, tell me about yourself, the first thing to say is your name.

143
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:41,750
Yes.

144
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:45,100
For example, my name is Sarah.

145
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:48,200
Or, simply, I'm Sarah.

146
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,870
Both are correct.

147
00:06:50,770 --> 00:06:53,170
It's always polite to start with your name.

148
00:06:54,690 --> 00:06:54,950
Right.

149
00:06:55,630 --> 00:06:56,730
My name is David.

150
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:03,420
So if we meet for the first time, we can say, my name is David.

151
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:04,960
I'm from Singapore.

152
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:09,450
Short, simple, and easy to remember.

153
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:11,550
Exactly.

154
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:16,600
And then you can add a small detail about your city or country.

155
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:20,670
For example, I'm from Toronto, Canada.

156
00:07:21,370 --> 00:07:24,130
It's a very friendly city with a lot of parks.

157
00:07:25,590 --> 00:07:30,280
Yes, giving one small detail makes your introduction interesting.

158
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:35,850
It can be about your hometown, a fun fact, or something you like.

159
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:39,460
Now, let's talk about age.

160
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:45,870
Some people don't like to share it, but in casual English conversations, it is normal.

161
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:48,760
Right.

162
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:50,900
I'm 32 years old.

163
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:53,440
And Sarah?

164
00:07:54,250 --> 00:07:56,350
I'm 29 years old.

165
00:07:57,270 --> 00:07:57,830
Very simple.

166
00:07:58,370 --> 00:08:00,440
Short, clear, friendly.

167
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:04,480
And now, we move to occupation.

168
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:09,800
Your job is important because it helps people understand your role.

169
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:12,650
So, Sarah, what do you do?

170
00:08:14,170 --> 00:08:15,130
I'm an English teacher.

171
00:08:15,150 --> 00:08:18,940
I teach students online and in classrooms.

172
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:23,620
I help them improve their speaking and confidence in English.

173
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:25,980
That's perfect.

174
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:28,970
And I'm a marketing executive.

175
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:43,240
See how adding one short detail about your job helps the listener know more about you?

176
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,810
It also gives them something to ask you next.

177
00:08:49,010 --> 00:08:49,330
Yes.

178
00:08:50,210 --> 00:08:55,360
For example, someone might ask, Oh, which products do you promote?

179
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:59,660
Then you continue the conversation naturally.

180
00:09:00,270 --> 00:09:01,090
Exactly.

181
00:09:01,730 --> 00:09:05,600
And remember, you don't have to explain everything at once.

182
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:07,940
One sentence is enough.

183
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:10,370
Okay, Sarah.

184
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:12,930
Now, let's talk about family.

185
00:09:13,730 --> 00:09:17,300
Family is a simple way to show a little personal side.

186
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,610
So, tell me about your family.

187
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:21,180
Sure.

188
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,590
I have a small family.

189
00:09:23,610 --> 00:09:28,110
It's just me, my husband, and my sister.

190
00:09:29,050 --> 00:09:33,380
We live in a small apartment and we like to cook together on weekends.

191
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:39,090
Cooking together is fun because we try new recipes and share laughs.

192
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:41,470
That sounds lovely.

193
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:43,720
I have a big family.

194
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:48,360
I have two brothers, one sister, and my parents.

195
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:53,190
We live in different houses, but we meet every weekend for lunch.

196
00:09:54,250 --> 00:09:57,230
Sometimes we go to the park or watch movies together.

197
00:09:58,350 --> 00:09:58,890
Yes.

198
00:09:59,730 --> 00:10:04,440
Sharing one small story about your family makes your introduction warmer and more interesting.

199
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:10,560
Even a tiny detail, like a weekend activity, helps the listener connect with you.

200
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:12,570
Exactly.

201
00:10:13,650 --> 00:10:17,390
After family, another friendly topic is pets.

202
00:10:19,970 --> 00:10:21,770
I have a cat named Coco.

203
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:24,580
She is very playful and fluffy.

204
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:30,720
Sometimes she sleeps on my laptop or jumps on my chair while I work.

205
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:35,130
It's funny and people enjoy hearing these small stories.

206
00:10:36,290 --> 00:10:36,930
That's cute.

207
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:40,760
I don't have a pet now, but I'd love a dog in the future.

208
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,290
I think dogs are friendly and fun.

209
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:45,850
Talking about pets is easy in English.

210
00:10:46,510 --> 00:10:52,180
I have a blank or I don't have blank, but I want blank.

211
00:10:53,350 --> 00:10:58,370
Yes, and you can add a short detail about the pet's personality or habits.

212
00:10:59,050 --> 00:11:04,980
For example, my dog loves going for walks in the park.

213
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:05,780
Hello, everyone.

214
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:06,540
Welcome.

215
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:12,850
Today, we are practicing how to answer the question, tell me about yourself.

216
00:11:13,730 --> 00:11:15,990
Listen carefully and repeat if you like.

217
00:11:16,810 --> 00:11:17,970
Yes, let's begin.

218
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:20,230
Tell me about yourself.

219
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:20,700
Sure.

220
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:22,540
My name is Daniel.

221
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,010
I am from the United Kingdom.

222
00:11:25,830 --> 00:11:27,850
I am 34 years old.

223
00:11:28,710 --> 00:11:31,000
I work as a business consultant.

224
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,780
I enjoy helping companies grow.

225
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,720
Nice to meet you, Daniel.

226
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:37,260
My name is Emma.

227
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:38,930
I am from Canada.

228
00:11:39,590 --> 00:11:40,850
I am 29 years old.

229
00:11:41,630 --> 00:11:43,350
I work as a marketing specialist.

230
00:11:44,030 --> 00:11:46,760
I help businesses promote their products.

231
00:11:46,990 --> 00:11:47,390
Great.

232
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:49,260
Tell me about your family.

233
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,080
I have a small family.

234
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:52,560
I have one sister.

235
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,180
I also have a dog.

236
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:56,450
I come from a big family.

237
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:59,590
I have two brothers and one sister.

238
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:01,540
And I have a cat.

239
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:02,860
Wonderful.

240
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,600
What do you like to do in your free time?

241
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:11,310
In my free time, I enjoy reading books and going for walks.

242
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:14,650
I like cooking and playing the piano in my free time.

243
00:12:15,330 --> 00:12:15,630
Nice.

244
00:12:16,490 --> 00:12:17,590
What is your favorite food?

245
00:12:18,350 --> 00:12:19,630
My favorite food is sushi.

246
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:20,690
What about you?

247
00:12:21,430 --> 00:12:23,330
My favorite food is pasta.

248
00:12:24,170 --> 00:12:25,140
And your favorite color?

249
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:27,680
My favorite color is blue.

250
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:30,120
My favorite animal is a dog.

251
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:32,180
My favorite color is green.

252
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:35,070
And my favorite animal is a cat.

253
00:12:35,850 --> 00:12:36,150
Great.

254
00:12:37,130 --> 00:12:38,530
Is there something you don't like?

255
00:12:39,490 --> 00:12:41,450
Yes, I don't like traffic.

256
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:43,660
I don't like loud places.

257
00:12:44,550 --> 00:12:45,370
Thank you for sharing.

258
00:12:45,410 --> 00:12:47,210
Now it's your turn.

259
00:12:47,970 --> 00:12:49,910
Tell us about yourself in the comments.

260
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:53,580
And don't forget to subscribe for more English lessons.

261
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,280
Let's continue.

262
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:59,450
Daniel, how long have you been working as a consultant?

263
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:03,790
I have been working as a consultant for eight years.

264
00:13:04,770 --> 00:13:06,520
I started right after university.

265
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:08,720
That's interesting.

266
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:11,010
I have been in marketing for five years.

267
00:13:11,670 --> 00:13:13,390
I really enjoy creative projects.

268
00:13:14,290 --> 00:13:16,900
Yes, creativity is important in marketing.

269
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,920
What do you like most about your job?

270
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:23,430
I like helping brands tell their story.

271
00:13:24,330 --> 00:13:31,500
It's

272
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:37,030
Today, we are going to focus on a very common question you will hear everywhere.

273
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,840
Tell me about yourself.

274
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:45,460
It might seem simple, but many learners find it tricky to answer clearly and confidently.

275
00:13:45,770 --> 00:13:46,500
Yes, David.

276
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:54,750
This question is asked in interviews, business meetings, networking events, and even casual conversations.

277
00:13:55,290 --> 00:14:02,250
So it's important to know how to answer in a way that's natural, friendly, and easy to understand.

278
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,220
Exactly.

279
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:05,640
Let's start at the very beginning.

280
00:14:06,490 --> 00:14:08,490
The first thing to say is your name.

281
00:14:09,190 --> 00:14:09,470
Yes.

282
00:14:10,090 --> 00:14:12,710
For example, my name is Sarah.

283
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:15,440
Or, just, I'm Sarah.

284
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:16,780
Both are correct.

285
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:18,500
Always start with your name.

286
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:20,600
It's polite and simple.

287
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:21,610
Great.

288
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:22,970
My name is David.

289
00:14:23,610 --> 00:14:27,870
So, when we meet for the first time, we can say, my name is David.

290
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:29,600
I'm from Singapore.

291
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:32,540
Short, simple, and friendly.

292
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:37,910
And you can add a small detail about your hometown or country.

293
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:41,370
For example, I'm from Toronto, Canada.

294
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:44,990
It's a friendly city with many parks and lakes.

295
00:14:45,910 --> 00:14:46,340
Exactly.

296
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:52,400
Small details make your introduction more interesting and give the listener something to comment on.

297
00:14:53,300 --> 00:14:54,870
Now let's talk about age.

298
00:14:55,610 --> 00:15:01,290
Some people don't share their age, but in casual conversation, it's okay.

299
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:01,860
Right.

300
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,870
I'm 32 years old.

301
00:15:04,630 --> 00:15:05,690
Sarah, how about you?

302
00:15:05,750 --> 00:15:07,830
I'm 29 years old.

303
00:15:08,430 --> 00:15:12,060
See, very simple, short, clear, and friendly.

304
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:16,280
Next, we move to occupation, your job.

305
00:15:17,010 --> 00:15:21,810
This is important because it helps people understand your role and what you do.

306
00:15:22,230 --> 00:15:22,650
Yes.

307
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:24,960
I'm an English teacher.

308
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:30,660
I teach online and in classrooms, helping students improve their speaking skills.

309
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:36,230
Adding a short detail about your job makes your introduction more engaging.

310
00:15:36,890 --> 00:15:37,270
Perfect.

311
00:15:37,890 --> 00:15:39,490
I'm a marketing executive.

312
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:44,420
I help companies grow their business online and reach more customers.

313
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:52,110
Even one short extra detail gives people something to ask about and continues the conversation naturally.

314
00:15:52,150 --> 00:15:52,930
Exactly.

315
00:15:52,950 --> 00:15:57,840
And remember, you don't need to give all the details at once.

316
00:15:58,630 --> 00:16:01,970
One sentence about your job is enough to keep it simple.

317
00:16:02,770 --> 00:16:03,500
Yes.

318
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:08,190
And after job, we can talk about family to add a personal touch.

319
00:16:08,590 --> 00:16:10,830
Sarah, tell me about your family.

320
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:11,880
Sure.

321
00:16:11,890 --> 00:16:13,840
I have a small family.

322
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:17,570
It's just me, my husband, and my sister.

323
00:16:18,430 --> 00:16:21,600
We live together and like to cook meals on the weekend.

324
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,360
It's a fun way to spend time together.

325
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:26,430
That sounds lovely.

326
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:27,730
I have a big family.

327
00:16:28,150 --> 00:16:31,160
I have two brothers, one sister, and my parents.

328
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:36,990
We don't live together, but we meet every weekend for lunch or a walk in the park.

329
00:16:37,790 --> 00:16:42,490
Sharing small stories about your family makes your introduction warm and friendly.

330
00:16:43,150 --> 00:16:49,180
Even one simple detail, like a weekend activity, helps the listener connect with you.

331
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:54,930
Okay, Sarah, now that we've talked about family, let's move on to pets.

332
00:16:55,370 --> 00:17:02,240
Pets are a fun topic because they show your personality and make your introduction more relatable.

333
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:05,320
Yes, I have a cat named Coco.

334
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,840
She's very playful and fluffy.

335
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:10,930
Sometimes she jumps on my desk while I work.

336
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:13,930
It's funny and makes me smile every day.

337
00:17:14,230 --> 00:17:15,130
That's so cute.

338
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:18,960
I don't have a pet right now, but I'd love a dog someday.

339
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:21,770
I think dogs are friendly and loyal.

340
00:17:22,470 --> 00:17:24,550
Talking about pets in English is simple.

341
00:17:25,290 --> 00:17:31,040
I have a blank or I don't have blank, but I want blank.

342
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:37,010
Yes, and you can also add a small detail about the pet's personality or habit.

343
00:17:37,650 --> 00:17:44,350
For example, my dog loves running in the park, or my cat likes to play with a ball.

344
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:45,290
Exactly.

345
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:47,970
And next, let's talk about hobbies.

346
00:17:48,730 --> 00:17:54,480
Hobbies show what you enjoy doing in your free time and give the listener a chance to connect with you.

347
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:56,420
I like reading books and cooking.

348
00:17:57,050 --> 00:18:00,310
Sometimes I try new recipes from different countries.

349
00:18:00,350 --> 00:18:05,210
It's relaxing, fun, and I often share my dishes with friends.

350
00:18:05,730 --> 00:18:07,910
I like traveling and watching football.

351
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:12,020
Traveling helps me learn about new cultures and meet new people.

352
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:15,720
And football is fun to watch with friends on the weekend.

353
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:18,440
Hobbies are great conversation starters.

354
00:18:19,090 --> 00:18:23,170
If someone likes the same hobby, you already have something to talk about.

355
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:30,800
Yes, and in English you can say, Hello everyone and welcome to today's English practice.

356
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:40,080
We are here to help you learn how to introduce yourself clearly and confidently in English.

357
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:47,580
Introducing yourself means saying who you are, where you're from, and what you do.

358
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:52,850
Take your time, listen, and repeat when you can.

359
00:18:53,890 --> 00:18:56,130
We are here to support you all the way.

360
00:18:57,150 --> 00:18:57,650
Are you ready?

361
00:18:58,730 --> 00:19:00,250
Let's start with greetings.

362
00:19:01,330 --> 00:19:03,160
Hello, nice to meet you.

363
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:05,240
Nice to meet you too.

364
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:10,080
This is polite and friendly when meeting someone new.

365
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:12,730
Now, let's talk about names.

366
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:15,310
My name is Olivia.

367
00:19:15,350 --> 00:19:17,630
I'm Olivia.

368
00:19:18,570 --> 00:19:19,760
Both are correct.

369
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,400
And my name is Thomas.

370
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:24,660
I'm Thomas.

371
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:26,620
Repeat after us.

372
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:30,890
My name is... Good job!

373
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:31,960
Next question.

374
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:33,940
Where are you from?

375
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:36,290
I'm from South Africa.

376
00:19:37,290 --> 00:19:38,950
I live in Cape Town.

377
00:19:39,870 --> 00:19:40,590
Explanation.

378
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,490
From means country.

379
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:47,400
Live means where you stay now.

380
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:50,180
I'm from Singapore.

381
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,380
I live in Singapore City.

382
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:57,070
Now you say your country and city.

383
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:58,870
Excellent.

384
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:01,860
Let's talk about work or study.

385
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:05,350
I work in business administration.

386
00:20:06,550 --> 00:20:10,470
I help manage company projects.

387
00:20:11,170 --> 00:20:13,140
Use simple sentences.

388
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:15,560
Clear is professional.

389
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:18,720
I work in customer service.

390
00:20:19,950 --> 00:20:23,050
I support clients and solve problems.

391
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:31,070
If you are learning or searching for a job, say, I am studying business English.

392
00:20:32,250 --> 00:20:35,790
Or, I am looking for work in marketing.

393
00:20:36,690 --> 00:20:37,170
Perfect.

394
00:20:38,170 --> 00:20:39,930
Simple and confident.

395
00:20:40,970 --> 00:20:41,840
Now family.

396
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:45,720
I am married and I have one son.

397
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:47,540
Explanation.

398
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:49,280
Brief information.

399
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:50,770
Not too personal.

400
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:52,770
I am single.

401
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:54,980
I live with my parents.

402
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:59,150
You can also say, I live alone.

403
00:20:59,190 --> 00:21:02,610
Or, I live with friends.

404
00:21:03,650 --> 00:21:07,460
Let's practice hobbies, things you like doing.

405
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:13,490
I enjoy going to the gym and cooking healthy food.

406
00:21:14,030 --> 00:21:17,850
I like watching documentaries and walking by the beach.

407
00:21:18,830 --> 00:21:19,570
Explanation.

408
00:21:19,610 --> 00:21:25,100
Use I like or I enjoy to talk about hobbies.

409
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:28,080
Now say your hobbies.

410
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:32,980
Hello, everyone.

411
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:36,230
Welcome to our business English practice session.

412
00:21:37,270 --> 00:21:42,840
Today, we will learn how to introduce yourself in simple, clear English.

413
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:44,350
Explanation.

414
00:21:44,390 --> 00:21:49,700
An introduction means telling people basic information about you.

415
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:51,800
Are you ready to practice?

416
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:53,510
Hi, everyone.

417
00:21:53,530 --> 00:21:55,110
I'm excited you're here.

418
00:21:55,170 --> 00:21:59,670
In business and daily life, you often need to talk about yourself.

419
00:22:00,410 --> 00:22:01,130
Explanation.

420
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:05,940
You introduce yourself in interviews, meetings, and new workplaces.

421
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:12,130
We will talk slowly, explain everything, and help you repeat.

422
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:12,920
Great.

423
00:22:13,710 --> 00:22:16,250
Let's begin with greetings.

424
00:22:16,270 --> 00:22:19,430
When you meet someone, you can say, Hello.

425
00:22:19,990 --> 00:22:20,800
Nice to meet you.

426
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:22,560
Explanation.

427
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:25,120
This is polite and friendly.

428
00:22:26,020 --> 00:22:26,770
Let's practice.

429
00:22:27,670 --> 00:22:28,010
Hello.

430
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:29,610
Nice to meet you.

431
00:22:30,510 --> 00:22:31,490
Nice to meet you, too.

432
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:33,130
Explanation.

433
00:22:33,190 --> 00:22:36,080
To means the same back to you.

434
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:38,140
Now you try at home.

435
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,330
So, first question.

436
00:22:40,970 --> 00:22:42,270
What is your name?

437
00:22:42,670 --> 00:22:43,410
Explanation.

438
00:22:44,130 --> 00:22:45,830
Always start with your name.

439
00:22:46,930 --> 00:22:48,300
My name is Daniel.

440
00:22:49,220 --> 00:22:49,560
And you?

441
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:50,900
What is your name?

442
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:52,660
My name is Sarah.

443
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:54,200
Explanation.

444
00:22:54,270 --> 00:22:58,310
Say, my name is not only Sarah.

445
00:22:58,370 --> 00:23:00,110
It sounds more polite.

446
00:23:00,910 --> 00:23:01,990
Let's repeat together.

447
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:05,040
My name is Sarah.

448
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:06,420
Wonderful.

449
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:12,190
When you introduce yourself, you can also say, I am Daniel.

450
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:13,400
Explanation.

451
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:19,150
I am is shorter and more casual, but both are correct.

452
00:23:19,770 --> 00:23:20,130
Yes.

453
00:23:20,810 --> 00:23:23,070
Some people say, I'm Sarah.

454
00:23:23,130 --> 00:23:24,550
Explanation.

455
00:23:24,610 --> 00:23:27,040
I'm is a contraction.

456
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:29,080
It is fast speech.

457
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:30,420
Repeat.

458
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:32,000
I'm Sarah.

459
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:34,680
Next, where are you from?

460
00:23:34,740 --> 00:23:36,680
I'm from Canada.

461
00:23:37,530 --> 00:23:38,190
Explanation.

462
00:23:38,930 --> 00:23:41,450
I'm from country, city.

463
00:23:42,340 --> 00:23:43,480
Where are you from?

464
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:45,570
I'm from Australia.

465
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:47,110
Explanation.

466
00:23:47,170 --> 00:23:50,400
Not I from Australia.

467
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:52,060
Remember the verb am.

468
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:54,140
Repeat.

469
00:23:54,990 --> 00:23:56,270
I'm from Australia.

470
00:23:56,310 --> 00:23:59,190
Some people like to add a city.

471
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:03,720
For example, I'm from Toronto, Canada.

472
00:24:03,860 --> 00:24:06,620
Or, I'm from Sydney, Australia.

473
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:08,040
Very good.

474
00:24:08,900 --> 00:24:10,160
Now, age.

475
00:24:11,140 --> 00:24:14,950
In business, you don't need to say your exact age.

476
00:24:15,870 --> 00:24:18,310
You can say, I'm in my 30s.

477
00:24:19,290 --> 00:24:21,190
Or, I'm in my 20s.

478
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:22,600
Explanation.

479
00:24:22,630 --> 00:24:27,080
This means an age range, more professional and private.

480
00:24:27,740 --> 00:24:27,980
Yes.

481
00:24:28,740 --> 00:24:28,960
Good.

482
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:32,120
Next, what do you do?

483
00:24:32,490 --> 00:24:34,980
This means your job or study.

484
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,720
I am a project manager.

485
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:42,090
I manage teams and business tasks.

486
00:24:42,110 --> 00:24:43,970
I am a marketing specialist.

487
00:24:44,690 --> 00:24:47,160
I help promote products and services.

488
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:48,600
Explanation.

489
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:52,750
Use I am a before your job title.

490
00:24:53,470 --> 00:24:57,170
If you are a student, say I am a student.

491
00:24:58,320 --> 00:24:59,820
I study business.

492
00:25:00,420 --> 00:25:02,480
or I study English.

493
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:07,150
I study plus subject.

494
00:25:07,950 --> 00:25:09,530
Let's ask about family.

495
00:25:10,530 --> 00:25:13,080
Do you live alone or with family?

496
00:25:13,100 --> 00:25:16,280
I live with my wife and our son.

497
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:19,420
I live with my parents and my sister.

498
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:24,790
I live with to describe people in your home.

499
00:25:24,850 --> 00:25:28,980
Or you can say, I live by myself.

500
00:25:29,530 --> 00:25:31,250
This means you live alone.

501
00:25:32,190 --> 00:25:33,380
Now, hobbies.

502
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:36,000
What do you like to do in your free time?

503
00:25:36,040 --> 00:25:38,340
I like cooking and reading.

504
00:25:38,380 --> 00:25:42,490
I enjoy hiking and listening to music.

505
00:25:43,570 --> 00:25:44,270
Explanation.

506
00:25:44,970 --> 00:25:49,220
I like and I enjoy both show hobbies.

507
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:50,960
Let's practice.

508
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,420
Say your hobbies now at home.

509
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:56,150
Very good.

510
00:25:57,110 --> 00:25:58,930
Next, favorites.

511
00:25:59,110 --> 00:26:00,370
What is your favorite food?

512
00:26:01,300 --> 00:26:03,080
My favorite food is sushi.

513
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:06,260
My favorite food is pizza.

514
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:07,920
Explanation.

515
00:26:08,550 --> 00:26:11,470
Favorite means the one you like the best.

516
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:13,870
What is your favorite color?

517
00:26:14,930 --> 00:26:16,760
My favorite color is blue.

518
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:19,540
My favorite color is green.

519
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:21,800
What is your favorite animal?

520
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:24,110
I like dogs.

521
00:26:25,050 --> 00:26:26,150
I like cats.

522
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:29,270
Also, talk about dislikes.

523
00:26:30,450 --> 00:26:32,210
I don't like being late.

524
00:26:33,070 --> 00:26:34,790
I dislike rude people.

525
00:26:34,810 --> 00:26:36,270
Explanation.

526
00:26:36,290 --> 00:26:42,360
I don't like and I dislike show negative preferences.

527
00:26:43,180 --> 00:26:47,770
Now, let's combine everything into a natural introduction.

528
00:26:48,650 --> 00:26:49,330
Listen first.

529
00:26:50,710 --> 00:26:53,030
Hello, my name is Daniel.

530
00:26:54,010 --> 00:26:55,170
I'm from Canada.

531
00:26:55,900 --> 00:26:57,260
I'm in my 30s.

532
00:26:58,480 --> 00:26:59,740
I am a project manager.

533
00:27:00,580 --> 00:27:01,800
I live with my family.

534
00:27:01,820 --> 00:27:02,610
Hello, everyone.

535
00:27:03,140 --> 00:27:05,890
Welcome back to our Business English podcast.

536
00:27:07,830 --> 00:27:12,220
Today, we are going to practice one very important question.

537
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:14,400
Tell me about yourself.

538
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:22,110
This question comes up in interviews, meetings, and even casual conversations.

539
00:27:23,710 --> 00:27:28,130
Many people think it's easy, but it can be tricky if you don't prepare.

540
00:27:29,590 --> 00:27:31,360
Yes, David, it's true.

541
00:27:31,380 --> 00:27:35,320
If you answer too short, people don't know much about you.

542
00:27:36,040 --> 00:27:38,770
If you answer too long, it can be confusing.

543
00:27:39,570 --> 00:27:44,170
So today, we'll show you a clear, simple, and friendly way to answer.

544
00:27:44,230 --> 00:27:46,360
Exactly.

545
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:48,940
Let's start at the very beginning.

546
00:27:50,990 --> 00:27:56,340
When someone asks, tell me about yourself, the first thing to say is your name.

547
00:27:57,440 --> 00:27:57,740
Yes.

548
00:27:58,580 --> 00:28:01,140
For example, my name is Sarah.

549
00:28:02,050 --> 00:28:04,190
Or, simply, I'm Sarah.

550
00:28:05,030 --> 00:28:05,850
Both are correct.

551
00:28:06,770 --> 00:28:09,170
It's always polite to start with your name.

552
00:28:10,670 --> 00:28:10,980
Right.

553
00:28:11,620 --> 00:28:12,700
My name is David.

554
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:19,400
So if we meet for the first time, we can say, my name is David.

555
